{"title":"Career Roadmap · Rehabilitation Professional (RCI)","role":"Rehabilitation Professional (RCI)","summary":"A Rehabilitation Professional works with persons with disabilities to support their education, functional development, participation, independence and inclusion.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Ed (Bachelor of Education)","Course":"B.Ed - Special Education"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Rehabilitation Professional works with persons with disabilities to support their education, functional development, participation, independence and inclusion."},{"type":"p","text":"In India, the Rehabilitation Council of India (RCI) regulates and maintains professional standards for specified rehabilitation and special-education professions. Therefore, this is a regulated career pathway: the student's exact qualification must be an RCI-recognized program, and the professional must meet the applicable registration requirements for the intended role."},{"type":"p","text":"A rehabilitation professional may work with children, adolescents or adults with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Intellectual disabilities"},{"text":"Specific learning disabilities"},{"text":"Autism spectrum conditions"},{"text":"Hearing impairment"},{"text":"Visual impairment"},{"text":"Locomotor disabilities"},{"text":"Multiple disabilities"},{"text":"Developmental disabilities"},{"text":"Other specified disabilities"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on the professional category, responsibilities can include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Functional assessment"},{"text":"Individualized education planning"},{"text":"Special education"},{"text":"Rehabilitation planning"},{"text":"Skill development"},{"text":"Family counselling/support"},{"text":"Assistive-technology support"},{"text":"Community rehabilitation"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Referral and multidisciplinary coordination"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Important qualification note","text":"“Rehabilitation Professional (RCI)” is a broad database label rather than one single profession. RCI recognizes different professional categories and programs. Students should choose the specific RCI-recognized course corresponding to the intended role and obtain the registration required for practice. A generic B.Ed without the required recognized special-education/rehabilitation qualification should not be represented as automatically qualifying for every RCI-regulated role."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Class 12","Relevant RCI-Recognized Special Education / Rehabilitation Program","Practical & Clinical / Field Training","RCI Registration / Applicable Professional Requirements","Entry-Level Rehabilitation Role","Rehabilitation Professional","Senior Professional","Rehabilitation Coordinator / Specialist","Program Manager / Clinical-Educational Leadership"]},{"type":"h","text":"Education-focused pathway"},{"type":"flow","items":["Special Education Qualification","RCI Registration","Special School / Inclusive School","Special Educator / Rehabilitation Professional","Senior Special Educator","Inclusion / Rehabilitation Coordinator"]}]},{"heading":"What You Learn During UG","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Foundations of Education & Disability"},{"type":"h","text":"Core areas"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Educational psychology"},{"text":"Human development"},{"text":"Child development"},{"text":"Learning theories"},{"text":"Foundations of special education"},{"text":"Inclusive education"},{"text":"Disability studies"},{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Educational technology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Disability awareness"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop foundational understanding of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Intellectual disability"},{"text":"Autism"},{"text":"Specific learning disabilities"},{"text":"Hearing impairment"},{"text":"Visual impairment"},{"text":"Locomotor disability"},{"text":"Multiple disabilities"},{"text":"Developmental disabilities"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional skills"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Ethical practice"},{"text":"Family interaction"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Special Education & Rehabilitation"},{"type":"p","text":"The student develops more specialized competencies."},{"type":"h","text":"Major areas"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Assessment"},{"text":"Individualized Education Plans"},{"text":"Special teaching strategies"},{"text":"Behaviour support"},{"text":"Functional assessment"},{"text":"Communication development"},{"text":"Life skills"},{"text":"Assistive technology"},{"text":"Inclusive classroom strategies"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Rehabilitation perspective"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Identify Functional Need","Assess","Set Goals","Plan Intervention","Implement","Monitor","Review"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Field Practice & Intervention"},{"type":"p","text":"Students should gain supervised experience."},{"type":"h","text":"Practical areas"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Educational assessment"},{"text":"Functional assessment"},{"text":"Individualized planning"},{"text":"Special teaching"},{"text":"Behaviour support"},{"text":"Communication support"},{"text":"Life-skills training"},{"text":"Family counselling/support"},{"text":"Assistive-device awareness"},{"text":"Community-based rehabilitation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Field settings"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Special schools"},{"text":"Inclusive schools"},{"text":"Rehabilitation centres"},{"text":"Early-intervention centres"},{"text":"Disability-service organizations"},{"text":"Community rehabilitation programs"}]}]},{"heading":"Final Year — Professional Rehabilitation Practice","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The final stage should integrate education, rehabilitation and multidisciplinary coordination."},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced skills"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Case documentation"},{"text":"Individualized intervention planning"},{"text":"Progress monitoring"},{"text":"Family participation"},{"text":"Transition planning"},{"text":"Vocational preparation"},{"text":"Assistive technology"},{"text":"Inclusive education"},{"text":"Community rehabilitation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Multidisciplinary collaboration"},{"type":"p","text":"A rehabilitation professional may coordinate with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Special educators"},{"text":"Psychologists"},{"text":"Speech-language professionals"},{"text":"Occupational therapists"},{"text":"Physiotherapists"},{"text":"Audiologists"},{"text":"Medical professionals"},{"text":"Social workers"},{"text":"Parents/caregivers"},{"text":"The exact responsibilities depend on the professional's qualification and scope."}]}]},{"heading":"Core Technical Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Skill Area","Key Competency"],"rows":[[{"text":"Special Education"},{"text":"Disability-specific teaching"}],[{"text":"Rehabilitation"},{"text":"Functional development"}],[{"text":"Assessment"},{"text":"Educational & functional assessment"}],[{"text":"IEP"},{"text":"Individualized planning"}],[{"text":"Behaviour"},{"text":"Positive behaviour support"}],[{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Accessible communication"}],[{"text":"Assistive Technology"},{"text":"AT selection/support"}],[{"text":"Life Skills"},{"text":"Functional independence"}],[{"text":"Family Support"},{"text":"Parent/caregiver collaboration"}],[{"text":"Inclusion"},{"text":"Inclusive education"}],[{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Case and progress records"}],[{"text":"Technology"},{"text":"Digital education tools"}],[{"text":"M&E"},{"text":"Progress monitoring"}],[{"text":"Ethics"},{"text":"Rights-based practice"}]]}]},{"heading":"Functional Rehabilitation Workflow","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Referral / Identification","Initial Assessment","Functional & Educational Assessment","Identify Strengths & Needs","Set Individual Goals","Intervention Plan","Implementation","Progress Monitoring","Family Review","Plan Modification","Transition / Follow-Up"]}]},{"heading":"Assessment Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Assessment should focus not only on limitations but also on strengths, participation and functional needs."},{"type":"h","text":"Areas"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cognitive/learning needs"},{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Academic skills"},{"text":"Social skills"},{"text":"Adaptive behaviour"},{"text":"Mobility/function"},{"text":"Self-care"},{"text":"Behaviour"},{"text":"Classroom participation"},{"text":"Vocational interests"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Assessment principle"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Strengths"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Needs"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Environment"},{"text":"+"}]},{"type":"flow","items":["Participation","Individualized Support Plan"]},{"type":"p","text":"Formal diagnosis should be made by appropriately qualified professionals; the rehabilitation professional uses authorized assessment tools and contributes to functional/educational planning within their scope."}]},{"heading":"Individualized Education / Rehabilitation Planning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong professional should be able to translate assessment findings into measurable goals."},{"type":"h","text":"Example structure"},{"type":"table","header":["Area","Current Level","Goal","Intervention","Measurement"],"rows":[[{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Limited functional communication"},{"text":"Improve functional requests"},{"text":"Structured communication activities"},{"text":"Weekly progress"}],[{"text":"Mathematics"},{"text":"Difficulty with basic operations"},{"text":"Improve accuracy"},{"text":"Adapted worksheets"},{"text":"Assessment score"}],[{"text":"Self-care"},{"text":"Needs assistance"},{"text":"Increase independence"},{"text":"Task sequencing"},{"text":"Independence level"}],[{"text":"Social Skills"},{"text":"Limited peer interaction"},{"text":"Increase participation"},{"text":"Structured group activities"},{"text":"Observation"}]]}]},{"heading":"Behaviour Support","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Professionals may work with students who exhibit:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Communication-related behaviours"},{"text":"Attention difficulties"},{"text":"Emotional dysregulation"},{"text":"Challenging behaviours"},{"text":"Difficulty with transitions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Positive support approach"},{"type":"flow","items":["Observe Behaviour","Identify Trigger / Context","Understand Function","Modify Environment","Teach Alternative Skill","Reinforce Positive Behaviour","Monitor Progress"]},{"type":"p","text":"The emphasis should be on safe, ethical and rights-based support, not punishment."}]},{"heading":"Assistive Technology","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Assistive technology can significantly improve participation."},{"type":"h","text":"Examples"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Communication boards"},{"text":"AAC systems"},{"text":"Screen readers"},{"text":"Magnification tools"},{"text":"Hearing-support technologies"},{"text":"Adaptive keyboards"},{"text":"Mobility aids"},{"text":"Educational software"},{"text":"Alternative input devices"}]},{"type":"h","text":"AT workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Identify Functional Need","Explore Options","Trial Technology","User / Family Feedback","Select Appropriate Support","Training","Monitor Effectiveness"]},{"type":"p","text":"The professional should collaborate with the appropriate specialist when the device requires specialized clinical or technical assessment."}]},{"heading":"Inclusive Education","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A rehabilitation professional can help schools move from simple placement toward meaningful participation."},{"type":"h","text":"Inclusive classroom model"},{"type":"flow","items":["Common Learning Goal","Identify Barriers","Adapt Instruction","Assistive Technology","Peer Support","Accessible Assessment","Progress Monitoring"]},{"type":"h","text":"Areas of adaptation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Content"},{"text":"Teaching method"},{"text":"Classroom environment"},{"text":"Learning materials"},{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Assessment"},{"text":"Time"},{"text":"Assistive technology"}]}]},{"heading":"Communication Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Depending on the disability population, professionals may need familiarity with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Visual communication"},{"text":"Simplified language"},{"text":"AAC"},{"text":"Sign-language awareness"},{"text":"Tactile/accessible communication"},{"text":"Social communication strategies"},{"text":"The professional should avoid assuming that every person with a disability communicates or learns in the same way."}]}]},{"heading":"Family & Caregiver Support","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Family collaboration is a major part of rehabilitation."},{"type":"h","text":"Responsibilities may include"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Explaining intervention goals"},{"text":"Demonstrating home-support strategies"},{"text":"Listening to caregiver concerns"},{"text":"Coordinating referrals"},{"text":"Sharing progress"},{"text":"Supporting transition planning"},{"text":"Connecting families with community resources"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Family partnership model"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Professional Expertise"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Family Knowledge"},{"text":"+"}]},{"type":"flow","items":["Person's Preferences","Shared Goals","Individualized Plan"]}]},{"heading":"Transition & Vocational Rehabilitation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As students move toward adulthood, rehabilitation becomes increasingly focused on independence."},{"type":"h","text":"Transition areas"},{"type":"l